From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyboolector.pyx: drop the Python 2 `long` check in Const()

`Boolector.Const()` guards its integer branch with
`isinstance(c, int) or (sys.version < '3' and isinstance(c, long))`. Cython
3.1 removed Python 2 support and with it the `long` builtin, so with the
`language_level=3` setup.py sets, cythonizing the module now fails with
`pyboolector.pyx:1277:70: undeclared name not builtin: long`. build.sh
installs the latest Cython unpinned, so every build hits it.

Keep only the `isinstance(c, int)` test, which is the only branch reachable on
Python 3. This is the same change carried by upstream's own
pyboolector-3.2.4.19342042739 sdist on PyPI, which was never committed to the
git repository.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [matches upstream's own 3.2.4.19342042739 PyPI sdist, never committed to git]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/src/api/python/pyboolector.pyx b/src/api/python/pyboolector.pyx
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/api/python/pyboolector.pyx
+++ b/src/api/python/pyboolector.pyx
@@ -1274,7 +1274,8 @@
                 Parameter ``width`` is only required if ``c`` is an integer.
         """
         cdef BoolectorConstNode r
-        if isinstance(c, int) or (sys.version < '3' and isinstance(c, long)):
+        # MSB:Remove sys.version < '3' to avoid unknwon type
+        if isinstance(c, int):
             if c != 0 and c.bit_length() > width:
                 raise BoolectorException(
                           "Value of constant {} (bit width {}) exceeds bit "\
